1
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:12,744
GPS › Analysis opens on the squad status: the latest value of every player, read against his own target.

2
00:00:12,744 --> 00:00:20,202
Amber is under target, green on target, red above. The median line gives you the squad’s reference.

3
00:00:20,202 --> 00:00:28,446
Filter by trainings or matches, and choose the period — from the last 7 days to the whole season.

4
00:00:28,446 --> 00:00:36,318
Click a value to open the player: his speed zones session by session, and his targets per band.

5
00:00:36,318 --> 00:00:43,418
Further down, internal load (sRPE) against external load (GPS): a widening gap is an early warning.

6
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:50,483
Matches reads every match against the player’s own recent form: the band is his usual spread.

7
00:00:50,483 --> 00:00:58,706
Pick a player at the top: one row per match, each value with its gap to his usual output.

8
00:00:58,706 --> 00:01:07,923
Comparisons puts two events side by side — here the last two matches, on the metrics you choose.

9
00:01:07,923 --> 00:01:15,009
Team averages first, then every player: who ran more, who sprinted less, and by how much.

10
00:01:15,009 --> 00:01:23,260
New data arrives through Imports — a file from your GPS system, or an automatic cloud sync on Pro.
